<title>UK: Unilever opens research centre in China.</title>
<headline>Unilever opens research centre in China.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Dutch food-to-households group Unilever Plc said on Monday it had opened its first scientific research centre in China.</p>
<p>Unilever said in a statement that the centre would look at how to match local consumer preferences with Unilever's brands.</p>
<p>The company first entered China in the 1920s and after a 33-year absence it re-entered the country in 1986.</p>
<p>Unilever has 12 joint ventures with Chinese partners with a turnover in China and Hong Kong of $500 million.</p>
<p>--London newsroom - +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
